  "description": "A dynaset over Pg (ORDER BY ID, fields ID and T1) is positioned on row 2 (MoveNext from the first record) and ID, T1 and Bookmark are read; then Execute with dbFailOnError grows Pg.T1 of row 2 by 60 characters on a second path of the same open; then ID, T1 and Bookmark are read again from the held cursor, MoveNext, MovePrevious, Requery and a MoveNext from the first record each read again. Asks what the held cursor and bookmark show after the row's page placement may have changed. Pg: 12 rows, ID and eight Text(255) fields T1..T8, each holding 61 repetitions of U+20AC (122 UTF-16 bytes of value; the character lies outside Latin-1). Images: 'before' (the fixture copy as given), then one kept image of the closed file after each step; every step opens the database read/write, makes one mutation and closes it, with the DBEngine still alive.",
